  "surprise": "P22 handoff x2 (every proj/fc2 weight and bias doubled, output-LN eps x4; the mirror of 133-claude's x0.5) on 153-claude scored 677/694/682 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 676/700/685: exact means 684.33 vs 687.00, -2.7, paired +1/-6/-3. Discard; inside the registered -35..+35 range, below its +5 central guess. The premise was wrong: branch_out_rms before the rescale was 0.025-0.034 (proj) and 0.036-0.042 (fc2), ABOVE the 0.02 init, not the predicted 0.006-0.012 Muon/decay equilibrium (fc2 outside the registered 0.004-0.03). So the frozen RL AdamW was already turning these matrices only ~1% per step, and x2 made that ~0.5%. Handoff logit drift was 0.125 on every seed: one bf16 ulp at |logit| 16-32, not the predicted <1e-2, but rounding-level. Held-out greedy at handoff was 0.969/0.957/0.972 (153: 0.9675), pretraining 4653/4342/4436 steps, final val 0.0876/0.0828/0.0805. Round 1 fell on every seed again: 652/450/506 targets vs 766/747/694 (mean -200). 133's x0.5 also lost round 1 on all three seeds, which is 6/6 across two function-preserving rescales, though 178's identical math once gave 259. RL caught up anyway: r1->r4 +509/+707/+664 vs 153's +391/+421/+497, final RL-solved 1161/1157/1170 (mean 1163 vs 1172), post-RL greedy 0.989-0.994. With 072/074/133 at x0.5 (-9/-10/-8) and this x2 at -3, the metric looks flat within noise for a 2x change in either direction of the RL step on the branch writes.",
